# CMS69 BMI Screening Cognitive Support Example
library "CMS69 BMI Screening GPG Strategy example".

/*
Clinical Reasoning Language (CRL) — v2.1.0 grammar reference example.

This file is the canonical small example. It models a **cognitive
support** workflow that supports a clinician in satisfying the
**CMS69 (BMI Screening and Follow-Up)** quality measure at point of
care, using a small set of BMI-related concepts and activities.

The full quality-measure encoding (Initial Population / Numerator /
Denominator / Exclusions / Exceptions) lives in
packages/crl/src/tests/fixtures/corpus/cms69/. This file shows
the cognitive-support facet: at an encounter, what should the clinician
do so the visit ends up in CMS69's numerator?

Surface conventions:
  - Case sensitive (keywords are lowercase: `concept`, `defined as`,
    `definition is`, `sem-or`, `sem-and`, `sem-not`, `or`, `and`, `not`,
    `library`, `include`, etc.).
  - Whitespace insensitive (indentation is decorative).
  - File starts with `#` + markdown-valid header line; the
    `library "Name".` declaration is REQUIRED in v2.1.0.
  - Quoted strings (`"..."`) are identifiers / refs to named declarations.
  - Backtick strings (`` `...` ``) are free text / evidence / system / code.
  - Single quotes (`'...'`) lex as UCUM units inside Quantity literals.

Statement types:
  - decision     — reusable decision logic; when/then/recommend|use
  - terminology  — valueset reference OR system+code(s) pair
  - activity     — executable clinical activity (CPG resource request)
  - concept      — clinical concept; one of three body kinds:
                     - `coded from` (asserted; ref is a valueset)
                     - `defined as` (composition over named concept refs)
                     - `definition is` (catalog-matched narrative predicate)

`defined as` body shapes:
  - bare ref:            `- defined as "X".`
  - record composition:  `- defined as ( "A" sem-and "B" ).` (value-preserving
                         sem-or/sem-and/sem-not set algebra over record operands; the
                         published cardinality is DECLARED via `shape is` — `Scalar` by
                         default — never inferred from the composition)
  - boolean composition: `- defined as ( not "A" and "B" ).` (scalar-boolean
                         and/or/not over scalar-boolean concepts — publishes a boolean; #189)
  - existence reduction: `- defined as exists ( "X" ).` (a scalar boolean:
                         does the RecordSet "X" contain any record? #189)

Bright line (#189): `sem-*` composes RECORDS (value-preserving), plain
`and`/`or`/`not` composes scalar BOOLEANS. A boolean parent over record leaves
is bridged EXPLICITLY via a `defined as exists ( … )` wrapper, never by an
implicit `sem-*`.

Narrative inside a `definition is` body uses lowercase `or` / `and` for
in-arg disjunction (e.g. `("Medical Reasons" or "Patient Declined Reasons")`),
which is distinct from the `sem-or`/`sem-and` in concept composition.
See docs/CRL Compilation Pipeline.md and the
project_sem-composition-operators memory for the rationale.

Optional fields:
  - `meta is` (repeatable) and `evidence is` on `concept`
  - `with` and `because` on `activity`
  - `do not perform` suffix on `request` keyword (activity)

Per v2.1.0 lock 026: under per-library scoping, bare refs are local to
the asking library. Cross-library refs use `"OtherLib"."Name"`. This
file is single-library so every ref below is bare.
*/

// ============ Decisions ============

// Top-level cognitive-support decision. Walked at every qualifying
// encounter for an adult patient. The when/then branches mirror CMS69's
// clinical flow:
//   1. document BMI if it isn't already recorded this period,
//   2. recommend a high-BMI intervention if BMI is high,
//   3. recommend a low-BMI intervention if BMI is low.
decision "CMS69 BMI Screening Strategy":

- when "Patient Eligible For BMI Screening" then:
  all:
  - when "BMI Not Documented During Measurement Period" then recommend activity "Document BMI".
  - when "Has Documented High BMI" then use decision "Recommend High BMI Intervention".
  - when "Has Documented Low BMI" then use decision "Recommend Low BMI Intervention".
  end.

// High-BMI sub-decision. Several intervention paths are CMS69-acceptable;
// `any:` says any one of these recommendations satisfies the measure.
decision "Recommend High BMI Intervention":
all:
- when "Patient Has Overweight or Obese Diagnosis" then:
  any:
  - recommend activity "Order Weight Assessment Referral".
  - recommend activity "Order High BMI Medication".
  end.
- when "Has Anti-Obesity Medication Contraindication" then recommend activity "Contraindicated Anti-Obesity Medication".

// Low-BMI sub-decision. CMS69 expects BOTH a follow-up order AND a
// documented care plan, so `all:` requires both recommendations.
decision "Recommend Low BMI Intervention":

- when "Patient Has Underweight Diagnosis" then:
  all:
  - recommend activity "Order Low BMI Follow-up".
  - recommend activity "Send BMI Care Communication".
  end.


// ============ Activities ============

// Activities are the executable side of a decision — what the cognitive
// support surface actually proposes to the clinician. Each `request` line maps
// to a CPG-on-FHIR proposal resource. `with`, `because`, and the
// `do not perform` suffix are optional.

activity "Document BMI":
- request CPGRecordInference.
- with "BMI as an Observation".

activity "Order Weight Assessment Referral":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with "Weight Assessment Referrals VS".
- because `Patient has documented high BMI without a current referral`.

activity "Order High BMI Medication":
- request CPGMedicationRequest.
- with "Anti-Obesity Medications VS".

activity "Order Low BMI Follow-up":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with "Low BMI Follow-up Service Requests VS".

activity "Send BMI Care Communication":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Document a follow-up care plan for low BMI`.
- because `CMS69 requires documented care planning when BMI is low`.

activity "Contraindicated Anti-Obesity Medication":
- request do not perform CPGMedicationRequest.
- with "Anti-Obesity Medications VS".
- because `Patient has a documented contraindication to anti-obesity pharmacotherapy`.


// ============ Terminologies ============

// Terminologies are either a valueset reference (used by `coded from`)
// or a single system+code pair (or repeatable codes).

terminology "BMI Range as a Condition":
- valueset is `urn:example:placeholder`.

terminology "BMI as an Observation":
- valueset is `BMI as an Observation`.

terminology "Height Valueset":
- valueset is `height valueset`.

terminology "Weight Valueset":
- valueset is `weight valueset`.

terminology "Overweight or Obese Diagnoses VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113762.1.4.1047.502`.

terminology "Underweight Diagnoses VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1563`.

terminology "Pregnancy Diagnoses VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.600.1.1623`.

terminology "Weight Assessment Referrals VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.600.1.1527`.

terminology "Anti-Obesity Medications VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1561`.

terminology "Low BMI Follow-up Service Requests VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.600.1.1528`.

terminology "Medical Reason VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1007`.

terminology "Patient Declined VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1582`.

terminology "Anti-Obesity Contraindication VS":
- valueset is `urn:example:placeholder`.

// A code-based terminology (system + code pair), useful when the
// reference is a single concept rather than a whole valueset.
terminology "Colonoscopy":
- system is `http://snomed.info/sct`.
- code is `73761001`.


// ============ Concepts ============

// --- Asserted concepts (coded from a terminology) ---

concept "BMI Range as a Condition":
- type is Condition.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "BMI Range as a Condition".

concept "BMI as an Observation":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- coded from "BMI as an Observation".

concept "Patient Height":
- type is Observation.
- value type is integer.
- coded from "Height Valueset".

concept "Patient Weight":
- type is Observation.
- value type is integer.
- coded from "Weight Valueset".

concept "Overweight or Obese Diagnoses":
- type is Condition.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Overweight or Obese Diagnoses VS".

concept "Underweight Diagnoses":
- type is Condition.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Underweight Diagnoses VS".

concept "Pregnancy Diagnoses":
- type is Condition.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- shape is RecordSet.
- coded from "Pregnancy Diagnoses VS".

concept "Pregnancy Diagnoses Exists":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Pregnancy Diagnoses" ).

concept "Weight Assessment Referrals":
- type is ServiceRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Weight Assessment Referrals VS".

concept "Anti-Obesity Medications":
- type is MedicationRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Anti-Obesity Medications VS".

concept "Low BMI Follow-up Service Requests":
- type is ServiceRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Low BMI Follow-up Service Requests VS".

concept "Medical Reasons":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- shape is RecordSet.
- coded from "Medical Reason VS".

concept "Medical Reasons Exists":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Medical Reasons" ).

concept "Patient Declined Reasons":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- shape is RecordSet.
- coded from "Patient Declined VS".

concept "Patient Declined Reasons Exists":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Patient Declined Reasons" ).

concept "Anti-Obesity Medication Contraindication":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Anti-Obesity Contraindication VS".


// --- Composition concepts: bare ref + sem-* composition shapes ---

// "BMI" composes three sources via sem-or (semantic composition —
// operands can be cross-typed; the composition layer reconciles).
// This is the value the rest of the file works with.
concept "BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- defined as
(
   "BMI Range as a Condition"
   sem-or
   "BMI as an Observation"
   sem-or
   "Calculated BMI"
).


// --- Predicate-kind concepts: narrative body + composing concept pair ---

// Predicates with narrative bodies are concepts with `definition is` bodies.
// A composing concept then references them as bare refs. This pair is
// the canonical "narrative + composer" shape.

concept "Most Recent BMI Selection":
- value type is Quantity.
- meta is `Selects the most recent BMI observation within the configured lookback`.
- evidence is `Calculated by Smile`.
- definition is most recent "BMI".

concept "Most Recent BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- meta is `Most recent qualifying BMI for the current encounter context`.
- evidence is `Calculated by Smile`.
- defined as "Most Recent BMI Selection".

// "Calculated BMI" preserves the BMI = weight / height² derivation
// chain. It composes the two source primitives (Height + Weight) via
// sem-and — semantic intersection at the composition layer. The
// `evidence is` text records the formula the implementation honors;
// the WHAT-vs-HOW principle keeps the formula out of the CRL grammar.
concept "Calculated BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- evidence is `Standard BMI formula: weight (kg) / height (m)^2`.
- defined as
(
   "Patient Height"
   sem-and
   "Patient Weight"
).


// --- Composition concepts: with sem-not ---

// `sem-not` is prefix unary; it negates the following operand or group.
// "BMI With Confirmed Height-Weight Source" requires BMI from a
// calculated source, NOT from a coded condition entry.
concept "BMI With Confirmed Height-Weight Source":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- defined as
(
   "Calculated BMI"
   sem-and
   sem-not "BMI Range as a Condition"
).


// --- Cognitive-support predicates (narrative bodies feeding the decision) ---

// Eligibility = "could this encounter satisfy CMS69?" The decision
// short-circuits when this is false. A boolean `not` over the Pregnancy
// existence wrapper carves out CMS69's denominator exclusion; `not` over the
// reason existence wrappers carves out the denominator exceptions. Each
// `... Exists` wrapper is `defined as exists ( "<RecordSet>" )` — the explicit
// existence reduction of the referenced `coded from` RecordSet (#189).
concept "Patient Eligible For BMI Screening":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   not "Pregnancy Diagnoses Exists"
   and
   not "Medical Reasons Exists"
   and
   not "Patient Declined Reasons Exists"
).

concept "BMI Not Documented During Measurement Period":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is without documented "BMI".

concept "Has Documented High BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "BMI" high.

concept "Has Documented Low BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "BMI" low.

concept "Patient Has Overweight or Obese Diagnosis":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Overweight or Obese Diagnoses" active.

concept "Patient Has Underweight Diagnosis":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Underweight Diagnoses" active.

concept "Has Anti-Obesity Medication Contraindication":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
// T13 / #94: the previous body `documented "Anti-Obesity Medication
// Contraindication"` is not a catalog pattern and emit-failed with an
// UnmatchedNarrative sentinel. Canonical form is `has <AssertedConcept>`
// against the asserted concept declared above (line 246, coded from
// "Anti-Obesity Contraindication VS"). See USER_GUIDE.md for the
// dimensionless-threshold convention and #94 for the documented-X gap.
- definition is has "Anti-Obesity Medication Contraindication".


// For deeper composition examples (deeply nested groups, AND NOT,
// in-arg disjunctions inside narrative bodies, and the full
// Initial Population / Numerator / Denominator structure), see the
// modeled measures:
//   packages/crl/src/tests/fixtures/corpus/cms22/
//   packages/crl/src/tests/fixtures/corpus/cms69/
